REGENT OF BIMA

PROVINCE OF WEST NUSA TENGGARA

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BIMA REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2019

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND

CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF BIMA,

Considering:
a. that every person including women and children has the right to the fulfillment of rights and protection from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in order to provide security and comfort;
b. that in the context of fulfilling the rights and protection of women and children from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in Bima Regency, the role of regional government is required in its implementation;
c. that the implementation of protection for women and children needs to be given direction and foundation to ensure legal certainty based on the principle of justice;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
6. Government Regulation Number 12 of 2017 concerning Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 6041);
7. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions as has been amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 927);
8. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for Women and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532);
9. Regional Regulation of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 8 of 2015 concerning Implementation of Women and Child Protection (Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province of 2015 Number 8, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 119);

With Mutual Approval

Article 2

The implementation of women's empowerment and child protection is carried out based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. victim protection;
e. best interests of the child;
f. survival and development of the child;
g. child participation; andh. benefit.

Article 5

1. Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in providing services for women and children experiencing problems of violence, discrimination, special protection, and other technical problems shall be implemented by UPTD P3AP2KB.
2. UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (1) shall carry out service functions:a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; andf. victim assistance.
3. In implementing the service functions as referred to in paragraph (2) letter b, a task force for women's empowerment and child protection may be established, facilitated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
4. Service functions provided by UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (2) shall refer to service standards that have been established in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 10

Strengthening and development of Women's Empowerment service provider institutions as referred to in Article 7 letter c shall be carried out through:a. improving the capacity of resources of Women's Empowerment service provider institutions at the regional level;
b. assistance in implementing Women's Empowerment services at the regional level;
c. development of Communication, Information, and Education for Women's Empowerment at the regional level;
d. strengthening networks among Women's Empowerment service provider institutions at the regional level;
e. facilitation of standardization implementation of Women's Empowerment service provider institutions at the regional level; andf. development of Women's Empowerment service provider institutions at the regional level.

Article 11

Implementation of protection of women shall be carried out by:a. prevention of violence against women involving parties in the Region;
b. provision of services for women victims of violence requiring coordination among Regional Apparatus, Vertical Agencies, and other institutions in the Region; andc. strengthening and development of women's protection service provider institutions in the Region.

Article 14

Provision of services for women victims of violence as referred to in Article 11 letter b shall be carried out through:
a. implementation of provision of services for women victims of violence through UPTD P3AP2KB or work units handling PPA affairs requiring coordination in the region;
b. provision of public complaint services for women victims of violence in the region;
c. provision of outreach services for women victims of violence in the region;
d. provision of case management services for women victims of violence at the regency level;
e. provision of temporary shelter services for women victims of violence in the region;
f. provision of mediation services for women victims of violence in the region;g. provision of assistance services for women victims of violence in the region;
h. provision of service facilities and infrastructure for women victims of violence in the region;
i. provision of information infrastructure available in public spaces; and
j. developing an emergency response system for acts of violence against women and children through applications.

Article 15

Strengthening and development of women's protection service provider institutions as referred to in Article 11 letter c shall be carried out through:a. improving the capacity of service providers for handling and protecting the rights of women victims of violence in the region;
b. provision of specific needs for women in emergency situations and special conditions in the region; andc. development of Communication, Information, and Education for protection of women's rights in the region.

Article 16

Implementation of improving the quality of family shall be carried out by:a. improving the quality of family in realizing gender equality and children's rights;
b. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of family in realizing gender equality and children's rights; andc. provision of services for families in realizing gender equality and children's rights.

Article 18

Strengthening and development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of family as referred to in Article 16 letter b shall be carried out through:a. improving the capacity of resources of service provider institutions for improving the quality of family in the region;
b. strengthening networks among service provider institutions for improving the quality of family in the region;
c. facilitation of standardization implementation of service provider institutions for improving the quality of family in the region; andd. development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of family in the region.

Article 23

The institutionalization of the fulfillment of Children's rights as referred to in Article 22 letter a is carried out through:
a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for the fulfillment of Children's rights in efforts to prevent violations of Children's rights in the region;
b. increasing participation and the role of children's forums or the like in the region; c. facilitating the strengthening of institutions and resources of government institutions, non-governmental, media and business sectors in the region;
d. facilitating the strengthening of networks among government institutions, non-governmental, media, and business sectors in the region; ande. strengthening cross-institutional cooperation among government, non-governmental, media, and business sectors to realize Child-Friendly Regency (KLA), Child-Friendly Sub-district (Kelana), and Child-Friendly Village (Dela).

Article 24

The strengthening and development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of children as referred to in Article 22 letter b is carried out through: a. capacity building of resources of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of children in the region;
b. assistance in the implementation of services for improving the quality of life of children in the region;
c. development of materials and implementation of Communication, Information, and Education on the fulfillment of Children's rights for service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of children in the region;
d. strengthening networks among service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the region;
e. facilitation of the implementation of standardization of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of Children in the region; andf. development of service provider institutions for improving the quality of life of children in the region.

Article 25

The implementation of Special Protection of Children is carried out by means of: a. prevention of violence against Children;
b. provision of services for Children who require special protection through coordination of parties both government and non-governmental institutions in the Region; andc. strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Children who require special protection in the Region.

Article 26

The prevention of violence against Children as referred to in Article 25 letter a is carried out through:
a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for the prevention of violence against Children who require special protection involving government and non-governmental institutions in the region;
b. provision of education on the prevention of violence against Children who require special protection in the region;
c. increasing community participation through the Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM) movement, business sector, media and children in the prevention of violence in the region; andd. strengthening cooperation to realize Child-Friendly Regency (KLA), Child-Friendly Sub-district (Kelana), and Child-Friendly Village (Dela).

Article 27

The provision of services for Children who require special protection as referred to in Article 25 letter b is carried out through: a. implementation of the provision of services for Children who require special protection through Regional Apparatus handling the affairs of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection and/or UPTD P3AP2KB in the region;
b. provision of public complaint services for Children who require special protection in the region;
c. provision of outreach services for Children who require special protection in the region;
d. provision of case management services for Children who require special protection in the region;
e. provision of temporary shelter services for Children who require special protection in the region;
f. provision of mediation services for Children who require special protection in the region;
g. provision of assistance services for children who require special protection in the region; andh. provision of facilities and infrastructure for services for children who require special protection in the region.

Article 28

The strengthening and development of service provider institutions for Children who require special protection as referred to in Article 25 letter c is carried out through:
a. capacity building of resources of service provider institutions for protection and handling of Children who require special protection in the region;
b. provision of specific needs for Children in emergency situations and special conditions in the region;
c. provision of Communication, Information, and Education on the protection of Children who require special protection in the region;
d. strengthening networks among service provider institutions for protection of Children who require special protection in the region; and e. facilitation of the implementation of standardization of service provider institutions for the protection of Children who require special protection in the region.

Article 34

The organization of CFC as referred to in Article 33 paragraph (1) shall be implemented in 5 (five) stages, namely:
a. CFC planning;
b. pre-CFC;
c. Regional Action Plan for CFC;
d. CFC implementation; ande. CFC evaluation.

Article 36

1. At the Pre-CFC stage, the Regional Government shall conduct a self-assessment of the CFC profile to determine the status of the Regional CFC before commencing the organization of CFC.
2. The self-assessment as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be based on the achievement of 24 (twenty-four) CFC Indicators included in the institutional and 5 (five) CFC clusters that have been established, namely: a. institutional;
b. cluster of civil rights and freedoms;
c. cluster of family environment and alternative care;
d. cluster of basic health and welfare;
e. cluster of education, leisure time utilization, and cultural activities;  andf. cluster of special protection.
3. The self-assessment as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by referring to the guidelines in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER VIII

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 44

1. The community, Family and/or parents may participate in the organization of women's empowerment and child protection. (2) The community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out individually or institutionally.
3. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out, among others, by:a. establishing women's empowerment and child protection units within community organizations, community-based child protection, or professional organizations;
b. conducting socialization regarding women's empowerment, prevention of violence against women and children, and child protection; c. conducting prevention of acts of violence in the community environment; andd. providing information and/or reporting the occurrence of violence, discrimination, exploitation, and human rights violations against women and Children to the competent authorities if violence against women and Children occurs in their environment;
e. optimizing the function of community organizations such as PKK, integrated service institutions for the protection of women and children in the Region; f. conducting socialization and education on laws and regulations related to women's empowerment, protection of women and Children, such as prevention of unregistered marriages and the dangers of child marriage;
g. providing input in the process of preparing laws and regulations in the region;
h. prohibiting the occurrence of unregistered marriages;
i. providing space for Children to gather and organize to express themselves and convey their opinions; andj. supervising Children in accessing various information.
